{"op":"add","path":"/elements/answer-text","value":{"type":"TextBlock","props":{"variant":"insight","content":"The jump month was March 2024, when net MRR rose by 9000. New subscriptions accounted for 7800 of the gain, expansion revenue for 2100, and churn offset the gross gain by -900. The Enterprise plan was the primary contributor, adding 4700 in net MRR. The dominant driver of the jump was the new mrr contribution component, as shown in the decomposition waterfall above."},"children":[]}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/methodology-text","value":{"type":"TextBlock","props":{"variant":"body","content":"This analysis used 36 records spanning 12 months and 3 plans. For each month, new MRR, expansion MRR, and churn MRR were summed across all plans. The month-over-month net delta was computed as the sum of new plus expansion minus churn. The month with the highest net delta was identified as the jump month, and its gross components were decomposed to explain the source of the gain. The per-plan breakdown shows how each plan contributed to the jump month total."},"children":[]}}
